---
/**
 * InsightCard — one article in the /insights directory
 * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * The card contents are brief §6, exactly and only: category, title, short
 * description, read link, and an OPTIONAL image. §6 also lists the visual
 * priority (1 title, 2 category, 3 description, 4 read link) — note that the
 * image is not in that list, which is the same statement the structure makes by
 * rendering it before the tag but giving it no visual weight of its own.
 *
 * ── WHY THE READ LINK IS A <span> ──────────────────────────────────────────
 * The whole card is one anchor, which is a far better target than a 90px link,
 * and `<a>` has a transparent content model so wrapping the `<h3>` is valid.
 * `<ArrowLink as="span">` renders the identical mark without nesting an anchor
 * inside an anchor — the same arrangement the homepage's `ArticleCard` and
 * `InsightsFeature` use.
 *
 * ── WHY `readLabel` IS A PROP, NOT A STRING IN THIS FILE ───────────────────
 * Every visible word on the site lives in `src/data/*.js`; a component that
 * types its own copy is how a page ends up with two wordings for one control.
 * The directory passes `directory.readLabel`.
 *
 * ── WHY NO DATE, AUTHOR OR READING TIME ────────────────────────────────────
 * §6 and §14 forbid invented publication dates, authors and statistics, and §12
 * says to display only fields that contain real information. Every article
 * record carries `publishedAt`, `updatedAt` and `readingTime` as `null` (see
 * `insights-articles.js`), so the fields exist for §12's data shape and no
 * markup is written for them. That is deliberate rather than unfinished: a
 * `<time>` element that can never render a value is markup without a subject,
 * and the day the first article is published the slot is added together with
 * the first real date. §6 does not list a date among the card's contents.
 *
 * ── WHY THE IMAGE IS CONDITIONAL ───────────────────────────────────────────
 * §6 lists the image and §7 says a clean card without one beats a poor stock
 * photo. No documentary photography exists yet, so every `imageKey` is `null`
 * and the branch never runs today. It stays because §12 and §14 ask the
 * structure to make a future article addable WITHOUT touching the page: giving
 * an article a picture is then a `media.js` slot plus one field here.
 *
 * ── WHY THERE IS NO LONGER A `data-article-category` MARKER ────────────────
 * That attribute was the category filter's hook: the chip row read it to decide
 * which cards to hide. The filter is gone (see `insights-page.js`), so the
 * attribute had no reader left, and an attribute nothing queries is the same
 * liability as a field nothing renders. The category still reaches the screen —
 * as the tag above the title, resolved through `categoryFor()`.
 *
 * ── THE CARD IS A BOX ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * `.in-card` is the surface: white, a hairline border, the site's 3px radius,
 * and a 2px lift with the border going to full ink on hover. That is the
 * presentation this directory was redesigned to, and the reason the card cannot
 * simply inherit the top-ruled row the page's other lists use.
 * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 */
import Media from '../Media.astro';
import ArrowLink from '../ArrowLink.astro';

interface Props {
  article: {
    slug: string;
    title: string;
    description: string;
    imageKey: string | null;
  };
  /** The article's category record — supplies the card's tag. */
  category: { slug: string; tag: string };
  href: string;
  /** The read link's label, from the page's data file. */
  readLabel: string;
}

const { article, category, href, readLabel } = Astro.props;
---

{/* A <li>: the grid is a <ul> because these twelve articles are a list, and the
    reveal device staggers a group's direct children. */}
<li class="in-card">
  <a class="in-card__link" href={href}>
    {article.imageKey && <Media imageKey={article.imageKey} ratio="3x2" zoom class="in-card__media" />}

    <span class="in-card__tag">{category.tag}</span>
    <h3 class="in-card__title">{article.title}</h3>
    <p class="in-card__desc">{article.description}</p>
    <ArrowLink as="span" label={readLabel} caps class="in-card__more" />
  </a>
</li>
